  "body": "**Stacked on #957** (#852): merged `issue/852-necked-tool-envelope` into this branch (0ea437f9), because both touch `crates/app/src/mcp/cutter_tools.rs` and `crates/tools/src/lib.rs`. Until #957 merges, this diff also shows #957's commit. #957 merges first.\n\nSlice 3 of #93: editing each milling tool kind by its parameters inside the outline editor (the Profile tab's Draw cutter view).\n\n## What changed\n- **Parameters in the outline editor** (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/tool_cutter_params.rs`). Above the points table, the Draw cutter view now shows the numbers each kind's outline is drawn from. They edit the same draft as the editor's fields, so the two always agree:\n  - every milling kind: cutter Ø, flute length, shank Ø, shank length, Neck (Ø and length);\n  - Ball nose / probe: ball R, shown read-only (d/2, #263);\n  - Bull nose: corner R;\n  - Drill: point angle;\n  - Chamfer mill: cone angle;\n  - End mill, tap, bore, torch: no tip parameter (a flat tip).\n- **The outline follows the parameters.** A Parametric outline is redrawn from the numbers, as before. A Custom outline is carried onto the new numbers by the new `camcraft_tools::cutter_fit::refit`:\n  - the tip inside the flutes is regenerated from the kind;\n  - whatever is drawn above the flute top keeps its shape and moves with the flute top;\n  - the shank top moves to the new one;\n  - the stated shank radius follows the new shank, and anything wider than the new shank is clamped to it.\n\n  The result is still judged live by `cutter_profile::check`. An edit that can't be carried is refused by name.\n- **The neck is a parameter of the outline.** `cutter_fit::necked` and `neck_of` handle it. `Tool` has no neck number, so the neck lives only in the drawn outline. A neck at or above the shank Ø, or not fitting inside the shank length, is refused by name.\n- **New undoable command `ReshapeTool`** (`crates/app/src/commands/tool_cutter.rs`). It lands the tool's numbers and its drawn cutter together, in one undo step:\n  - every `ChangeTool` law runs on the new numbers (`ChangeTool::judged`, with the stale-cutter agreement skipped);\n  - the outline is judged against the **new** numbers.\n\n  Apply cutter queues it when the draft numbers moved (otherwise `SetToolCutter`, as before). The editor's Apply queues it when a drawn cutter is landed and the edit changes a number the outline is drawn to, carrying the landed outline. Before this, such an edit was refused (\"reset the cutter profile to Parametric first\"). `ChangeTool` alone is unchanged and still refuses.\n- **MCP:** new `set_tool_cutter_params` (any of diameter / corner_r / tip_angle / flute_len / shank_d / shank_len, plus `neck` `{diameter, length}` | null | omitted). It runs the same `ReshapeTool`. `get_tool_cutter_profile` now also reports `neck`.\n- Decisions: `docs/decisions/93-outline-param-editing.md`.\n\n## Tests\n- `camcraft-tools` `cutter_fit::tests` (4 tests): every shape edit (diameter, flute length, shank length and Ø, a retype to ball, bull, drill or chamfer) carries a hand-drawn neck and still passes `check`; every catalog milling tool carries its own outline onto new numbers; unchanged numbers leave the drawing alone; a narrower shank clamps it; the neck round-trips; and the neck refusals.\n- `crates/app/tests/tool_cutter_params.rs` (3 tests, new binary): `a_parameter_edit_carries_the_drawn_cutter_in_one_undo_step`, `a_reshape_is_refused_by_name_against_the_new_numbers`, `the_tool_is_edited_by_its_parameters_over_mcp`.\n- `egui_app::tests::tool_cutter_params` (5 tests): the per-kind parameters, Parametric redraw and Custom carry, the neck refusal by name, Apply cutter's one undo step, and the editor's Apply carrying a landed cutter.\n- Structural twin: `egui_app::tests::structural::tool_cutter_params_structure`.\n- The slice 2 suites (`tool_cutter_profile`, `egui_app::tests::tool_cutter`, `tool_profile`) still pass.\n- No snapshot PNG was changed.\n- Quick gate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` on the final head: green (tools, app 461 s, ui 55 s; 0 failed), plus `cargo clippy -p camcraft-tools -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -D warnings` clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n- No hand check in the GUI: the window's taller third column was checked only through AccessKit placement, not by eye.\n- The camcraft-mcp skill's tool table doesn't list the new tool. It is a process file, so updating it needs a PROCESS_VERSION bump; I left it alone, the same as slice 2.\n- The simulation and collision feed of the drawn profiles is #852 / PR #957; that seam is untouched.\n\n## MCP\nThe new user-facing command `ReshapeTool` ships with its MCP tool, `set_tool_cutter_params`. Editing and deleting a tool by its full definition over MCP stays #734.\n\nChangelog: Tool editor: edit a milling tool by its parameters (diameter, tip, flutes, shank, neck) inside the Draw cutter view; a drawn cutter follows the numbers instead of blocking the edit, landed with them in one undo step; MCP `set_tool_cutter_params` (#93)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFork synced at v0.17.0 (branched from upstream/main f490458a).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nRefs #93",
